2026-10-16T03:17:32.5581073Z   ISSUE_NUMBER: 55931
2026-10-16T03:17:32.5581282Z   ISSUE_TITLE: [FEATURE]:[desktop] Windows installer should let users choose the installation directory
2026-10-16T03:17:32.5583801Z   ISSUE_BODY: ### Feature hasn't been suggested before.

- [x] I have verified this feature I'm about to request hasn't been suggested before.

### Describe the enhancement you want to request

## Summary
The Windows desktop build only ships `opencode-desktop-win-x64.exe`. Double-clicking it silently installs to `%LOCALAPPDATA%\Programs\opencode-desktop`, with no UI and no way for the user to choose the installation directory.

## Steps to reproduce
1. Download `opencode-desktop-win-x64.exe` from the releases page
2. Double-click it
3. No installer UI appears; the app ends up in `%LOCALAPPDATA%\Programs\opencode-desktop`

## Expected behavior
The installer should let the user pick the installation path (an assisted installer with a "Destination Folder" step), so a ~120 MB Electron app can be installed to another drive or a user-managed location.

## Proposed change
```yaml
nsis:
  oneClick: false
  allowToChangeInstallationDirectory: true
```
This turns the silent one-click installer into an assisted installer with a destination-folder page. Install scope, auto-update, and the uninstall entry can stay unchanged.

## Environment
- OS: Windows 10 Home China 22H2 (build 19045.7548)
- opencode desktop: 2.0.30 (exe product/file version)
- Asset: opencode-desktop-win-x64.exe

## Additional context
macOS also ships `opencode-desktop-mac-{arm64,x64}.zip`, while Windows has no comparable artifact, so there is currently no user-controllable install path on Windows at all. A portable/zip target would complement the fix, but the directory picker is the primary request.
